          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: lo spumante",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lo spumante — \"the sparkling wine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A mezzanotte apriamo lo spumante. At midnight we open the sparkling wine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on spuma, ‘foam’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "spumante is the present participle of spumare \"to foam\", from Latin spūma \"foam\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
